From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winevulkan: Skip time domain queries for managed swapchains.

Managed cross-process swapchains (0001) are created without a host
swapchain, so their host handle is VK_NULL_HANDLE. win32u already handles
them in vkGetSwapchainTimingPropertiesEXT, vkSetSwapchainPresentTiming-
QueueSizeEXT and vkGetPastPresentationTimingEXT, but
vkGetSwapchainTimeDomainPropertiesEXT is implemented in winevulkan and
passed the null handle to the driver.

vkd3d-proton queries the time domains when the swapchain is created and
whenever its timing counters change. On NVIDIA this crashes in the driver
(__pthread_rwlock_rdlock on a null object, from libnvidia-glcore). Arc
Raiders hits it when the game window is unfocused while a level loads,
which is presumably when its swapchain takes the managed path.

Report no time domains for a swapchain without a host swapchain, like the
zeroed timing properties win32u returns for it. vkd3d-proton then does not
use present timing for that swapchain.

Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/891

Not runtime-tested.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winevulkan/vulkan.c b/dlls/winevulkan/vulkan.c
--- a/dlls/winevulkan/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/winevulkan/vulkan.c
@@ -768,6 +768,15 @@
 
     TRACE("device %p, swapchain %p, properties %p, counter %p\n", device, swapchain, properties, counter);
 
+    /* Managed (cross-process dmabuf) swapchains have no host swapchain and no
+     * present timing, matching win32u's vkGetSwapchainTimingPropertiesEXT. */
+    if (!swapchain->host.swapchain)
+    {
+        properties->timeDomainCount = 0;
+        if (counter) *counter = 0;
+        return VK_SUCCESS;
+    }
+
     host_properties.timeDomainCount = 0;
     host_properties.pTimeDomainIds = NULL;
     host_properties.pTimeDomains = NULL;
